{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MotivicSubstrate","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MotivicSubstrate","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Prime.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Localization.Basic"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MotivicSubstrate.nonarchimedean_nontrivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MotivicSubstrate.nonarchimedean_nontrivial","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MotivicSubstrate.lean#L92-L92","doc":"**Substrate axiom (non-archimedean non-degeneracy).**  At\nleast one finite place `p` has a non-trivial realization\ntarget.\n\nRef: [tate1967]. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MotivicSubstrate.archimedean_nontrivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MotivicSubstrate.archimedean_nontrivial","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MotivicSubstrate.lean#L86-L86","doc":"**Substrate axiom (archimedean non-degeneracy).**  The\narchimedean realization target is nontrivial.\n\nRef: [tate1967]. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MotivicSubstrate.realize","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MotivicSubstrate.realize","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MotivicSubstrate.lean#L81-L81","doc":"The realization functor at place `v`, taking values in the\ntarget ring `Target v`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MotivicSubstrate.lefschetz_invertible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MotivicSubstrate.lefschetz_invertible","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MotivicSubstrate.lean#L78-L78","doc":"`𝕃` is invertible in `𝓜̂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MotivicSubstrate.inclusion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MotivicSubstrate.inclusion","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MotivicSubstrate.lean#L76-L76","doc":"Canonical inclusion `K₀ → 𝓜̂` of the Grothendieck ring into\nthe dimension-completed localization. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MotivicSubstrate.lefschetz","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MotivicSubstrate.lefschetz","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MotivicSubstrate.lean#L73-L73","doc":"The Lefschetz motive `𝕃 = [𝔸¹] ∈ K₀(Var_k)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MotivicSubstrate.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MotivicSubstrate.mk","kind":"ctor","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MotivicSubstrate.lean#L69-L69","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MotivicSubstrate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MotivicSubstrate","kind":"class","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MotivicSubstrate.lean#L52-L93","doc":"**The motivic substrate** (axiomatic class).\n\n`MotivicSubstrate K0 Mhat Target` axiomatises the QOU motivic\nsubstrate over:\n* `K0` — the Grothendieck ring `K₀(Var_k)`.\n* `Mhat` — the dimension-completed localization\n  `𝓜̂ = K₀[𝕃⁻¹]^∧`.\n* `Target : Place → Type*` — the realization target at each\n  place (e.g. `ℝ` at `∞`, `ℚ_p` at finite primes).\n\nSubstrate axioms (paired place compatibility): the realization\ntarget is nontrivial at the archimedean place AND at some\nfinite place — the minimal non-vacuous fragment of the Tate\nfactorisation `ρ_tot([X]) = (ρ_v([X]))_v` of\n`def:adelic-substrate`.\n\nRef: [kontsevich1995], [denef-loeser2001], [tate1967]. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:motivic-substrate","label":"def:motivic-substrate","md":"quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/motivic-substrate.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.instDecidableEqPlace.decEq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.instDecidableEqPlace.decEq","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MotivicSubstrate.lean#L50-L50","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.instDecidableEqPlace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.instDecidableEqPlace","kind":"instance","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MotivicSubstrate.lean#L50-L50","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Place.finite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Place.finite","kind":"ctor","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MotivicSubstrate.lean#L49-L49","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Place.infty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Place.infty","kind":"ctor","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MotivicSubstrate.lean#L48-L48","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Place","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Place","kind":"inductive","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MotivicSubstrate.lean#L43-L50","doc":"A **place** of `ℚ`: either the archimedean place `∞` or a\nfinite prime `p`. The `finite` constructor takes a\n`Nat.Primes` value (Mathlib subtype `{p : ℕ // p.Prime}`) so\nthat non-prime indices are ruled out at the type level. ","signatureChunk":0}]}